  {
   "id": "resistive-switching-test",
   "title": "Resistive switching test circuit",
   "page": 5,
   "description": "Measures the switching times. A gate pulse drives the DUT gate through Rg; the drain is loaded by RL to the Vdd supply and the source is grounded. VGS is read at the gate and VDS at the drain. The switching rows use VGS = 10 V, VDS = 15 V, RL = 2.6 Ω, RGEN = 3 Ω. td(on) runs from 10 % of the rising gate pulse to the point where VDS has fallen to 90 %; tr is the VDS fall from 90 % to 10 %; ton is their sum. td(off) runs from 90 % of the falling gate pulse to VDS rising through 10 %; tf is the VDS rise from 10 % to 90 %; toff is their sum.",
