  {
   "id": "diode-recovery-test",
   "title": "Diode recovery test circuit",
   "page": 5,
   "description": "Measures the body diode's reverse recovery. The DUT has its gate tied to its source, so only its body diode conducts; it sits across the inductor L between the Vdd supply and the drain of a second, switching MOSFET whose gate is pulsed by Ig. With the switch's gate low the DUT body diode carries IF; when the gate goes high the diode current falls at dI/dt, reverses, and recovers while Vds rises to Vdd. A current sensor in the DUT source lead reads Isd; Vds is taken across the DUT. The recovery rows use IF = 5.7 A, dI/dt = 100 A/µs. trr is the recovery time and IRM the peak reverse current; Qrr is the area of the reverse current.",
