 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Threshold is 0.65 to 1.45 V at 250 µA. On-resistance is guaranteed at three gate voltages: 26.5 mΩ max at 10 V and 5.7 A, 32 mΩ at 4.5 V and 5 A, 48 mΩ at 2.5 V and 3 A. With 4.5 V on the gate and 5 V across it the channel delivers at least 30 A. The gate is rated ±12 V and has 1.5 to 4.5 Ω of internal resistance."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "On-resistance rises with junction temperature: at 10 V drive and 5.7 A it is 18 mΩ typical (26.5 mΩ max) at 25 °C and 28 mΩ typical (38 mΩ max) at 125 °C; Figure 4 shows about 1.7 times the 25 °C value at 150 °C. In Figure 2 the 125 °C transfer curve conducts at a lower gate voltage than the 25 °C curve."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 1.4 W rating rests on the t ≤ 10 s junction-to-ambient figure (90 °C/W max) with TJ(MAX) at 150 °C. Steady state on a 1 in² 2 oz copper pad the junction-to-ambient resistance is 125 °C/W max, of which up to 80 °C/W is junction to lead. At 70 °C ambient the limits are 4.7 A and 0.9 W."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pulsed operation",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "The 30 A pulsed rating is repetitive and limited by the junction reaching 150 °C. Figures 9 to 11 give single-pulse safe operating area, single-pulse power and transient thermal impedance on the 1 in² FR-4 board."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The source-to-drain body diode carries up to 2 A continuously and drops 0.7 V typical, 1 V max, at 1 A. Reverse recovery at 5.7 A and 100 A/µs takes 8.5 ns and 2.6 nC typical."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Listed uses are load switches and PWM circuits."
  }
 ]
